    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Prime Minister and Minister of Finance, Minister ofBuddhasasana, Religious & Cultural Affairs and Minister of UrbanDevelopment & Housing on 22nd of September, 2020\n\n(Published in the Gazette on September 04, 2020)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPrice : Rs. 6.00Postage : Rs. 15.00\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\n[Bill No. 1]\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nNATION BUILDING TAX (AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Nation Building Tax Act, No. 9 of 2009\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECTClause 2 : This clause amends section 3 of the Nation Building Tax Act, No. 9 of 2009and the legal effect of the section as amended is to limit the period of application of theNation Building Tax under the said Act to the period prior to December 1, 2019.\n\nNation Building Tax (Amendment)1\n\n5\n\n10\n\nShort title.\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 59/2019\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE NATION BUILDING TAXACT, NO. 9 OF 2009\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows: -\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Nation Building Tax(Amendment) Act, No. of 2020.\n\n2.Section 3 of the Nation Building Tax Act, No. 9 of2009 as last amended by Act, No. 20 of 2019, is herebyfurther amended in subsection (1) by the substitution for thewords, \u201cbe charged from every person\u201d, of the words andfigures \u201cbe charged prior to December 1, 2019, from everyperson\u201d.\n\n3. In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nAmendmentof section 3of Act,No. 9 of2009.\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency.\n\n2Nation Building Tax (Amendment)\n\nDEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING"
