    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Justice on 13th of November, 2020\n\n(Published in the Gazette on September 02, 2019)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\n2-2dp\n\n2-\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPrice : Rs. 17.00Postage : Rs. 15.00\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\n[Bill No. 12]\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPENAL CODE (AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Penal Code (Chapter 19)\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClauses 2 to 30: These clauses make provisions to amend the Penal Code (Chapter 19)by replacing outdated words and expressions appearing in that Code with the words andexpressions which reflect the contemporary position.\n\nPenal Code (Amendment)1\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 43/2016\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE PENAL CODE ( CHAPTER 19 )\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:-\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Penal Code(Amendment) Act, No. of 2020.\n\n2.The word \u201cCeylon\u201d, wherever it appears in the PenalCode (Chapter 19) (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipalenactment\u201d) other than in sections 3, 18A, 120, 138, 158,159, 160, 225 and 256A thereof, shall be substituted with theword \u201cSri Lanka\u201d.\n\n3.The word \u201cQueen\u201d, wherever it appears in theprincipal enactment, other than in sections 19, 115 and 120thereof, shall be substituted with the word \u201cRepublic\u201d.\n\n4.Section 12 of the principal enactment is herebyrepealed and the following section is substituted therefor:-\n\n12. The word \u201cRepublic\u201d denotes theDemocratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka.\u201d.\n\n5.Section 13 of the principal enactment is herebyrepealed.\n\n6.Section 14 of the principal enactment is herebyrepealed and the following section is substituted therefor:-\n\n14. The word \u201cGovernment\u201d, where noother meaning is indicated by any descriptiveor qualifying words or by the context, and the\n\nShort title."
