    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 56]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nPresented by the Minister of Finance on 09th of July, 2021\n\n(Published in the Gazette on June 28, 2021)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\nSECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION OFSRI LANKA\n\nto establish the Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka; toregulate market institutions, certain public offers of securities, marketintermediaries; to protect investors and to provide for enforcementmeasures; to deal with market misconduct; and to overcome the challengesencountered by securities market regulators and to repeal the Securitiesand Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka Act, No. 36 of 1987 and for matters connected therewith or incidental thereto\n\nPrice : Rs. 247.00Postage : Rs. 120.00\n\n1Securities and Exchange Commission ofSri Lanka\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 8/2017\n\nAN ACT TO ESTABLISH THE SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION OFSRI LANKA; TO REGULATE MARKET INSTITUTIONS, CERTAIN PUBLIC\n\nOFFERS OF SECURITIES, MARKET INTERMEDIARIES; TO PROTECT\n\nINVESTORS AND TO PROVIDE FOR ENFORCEMENT MEASURES; TO DEAL\n\nWITH MARKET MISCONDUCT; AND TO OVERCOME THE CHALLENGES\n\nENCOUNTERED BY SECURITIES MARKET REGULATORS AND TO REPEAL\n\nTHE SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION OF SRI LANKA ACT,NO. 36 OF 1987 AND FOR MATTERS CONNECTED THEREWITH OR\n\nINCIDENTAL THERETO.\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows: -\n\n1.(1) This Act may be cited as the Securities andExchange Commission of Sri Lanka Act, No \u2026.. of 2021.\n\n(2) The provisions of this Act, other than this section,shall come into operation on such date or dates as the Ministermay appoint by Order published in the Gazette. Differentdates may be appointed by the Minister for the coming intooperation of different Parts of this Act."
