    "chunk_size_bytes": 2030,
    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPart II of July 16, 2021\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 19.07.2021)\n\nTo be presented in Parliament by Hon. Sarathi Dushmantha, M.P.for Kegalle District\n\nPrice : Rs. 17.00Postage : Rs. 15.00\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nThis Gazette Supplement can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nA\n\nto incorporate the Balangoda Ananda Maitreya Foundation\n\n(Private Members\u2019 Bill)\n\nBALANGODA ANANDA MAITREYA FOUNDATION(INCORPORATION)\n\n1Balangoda Ananda Maitreya Foundation(Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\nShort title\n\nAN ACT TO INCORPORATE THE BALANGODA ANANDA MAITREYAFOUNDATION\n\nWHERE A Foundation called and known as the \u201cBalangodaAnanda Maitreya Foundation\u201d has heretofore been formedin Sri Lanka for the purpose of effectually carrying out andtransacting all objects and matters connected with the saidFoundation according to the rules agreed to by its members :\n\nAND WHEREAS the said Foundation has heretoforesuccessfully carried out and transacted the several objectsand matters for which it was formed, and has applied to beincorporated and it will be for the public advantage to grantsuch application :\n\nBE it therefore enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows :\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Balangoda AnandaMaitreya Foundation (Incorporation) Act, No. of 2021\n\n2.From and after the date of commencement of thisAct, such and so many persons as now are members of the\u201cBalangoda Ananda Maitreya Foundation\u201d (hereinafterreferred to as the \u201cfoundation\u201d) or shall hereafter be admittedas members shall be a body corporate (hereinafter referred toas the \u201cCorporation\u201d) with perpetual succession, under thename and style of \u201cBalangoda Ananda Maitreya Foundation\u201dand by that name may sue and be sued in all courts, with fullpower and authority to have and use a common seal and toalter the same at its pleasure."
