    "chunk_text": "2.From and after the date of commencement of thisAct, such and so many persons as now are members of the\u201cBalangoda Ananda Maitreya Foundation\u201d (hereinafterreferred to as the \u201cfoundation\u201d) or shall hereafter be admittedas members shall be a body corporate (hereinafter referred toas the \u201cCorporation\u201d) with perpetual succession, under thename and style of \u201cBalangoda Ananda Maitreya Foundation\u201dand by that name may sue and be sued in all courts, with fullpower and authority to have and use a common seal and toalter the same at its pleasure.\n\n(a)to assist the most Venerable Aggamahapanditha,Adhiraja Maha Rattaguru Balangoda Ananda\n\nPreamble\n\nGeneralobjects of theCorporation\n\nIncorporationof theBalangodaAnandaMaitreyaFoundation20\n\n25\n\nBalangoda Ananda Maitreya Foundation(Incorporation)2\n\nMaitreya Maha Nayake Thero in his effect ofdisseminating the Buddha, Dhamma and BuddhistPhilosophy in Sri Lanka and abroad ;\n\n(b)to publish old and new publications, books,writings, reports and information on most VenerableAggamahapanditha, Adhiraja Maha RattaguruBalangoda Ananda Maitreya Maha Nayake Theroand such other material written on him by others onthe approval of the Foundation;\n\n(c)to establish and maintain liaison with countries andinternational organizations, on the Buddha,Dhamma, Buddhist Philosophy and teachings ofLoad Buddha;\n\n(d)to establish an information centre/research libraryin order to collect and designation information onteachings of the Lord Buddha, publication andspeeches of the most VenerableAggamahapanditha, Adhiraja Maha RattaguruBalangoda Ananda Maitreya Maha Nayake Theroon Buddhism and its doctrine ;\n\n(e)to establish an International Language School inSri Lanka for the benefit of the Bhikkhus of SriLanka and abroad;\n\n(f)to establish a fund to provide facilities andassistance to Bhikkhus selected by the Foundationfrom Sri Lanka and abroad;\n\n(g)to sponsor and conduct conferences, seminars,workshops, ground studies, lectures in Sri Lanka orelsewhere;"
