    "chunk_text": "BE it therefore enacted by Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Kelaniya BuddhistWomen's Charitable Society (Incorporation) Act, No. of2021.\n\nIncorporationof theKelaniyaBuddhistWomen'sCharitableSociety\n\n2Kelaniya Buddhist Women's Charitable Society\n\n(Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n3. The general objects for which the Corporation isconstituted are hereby declared to be\u2014\n\n(a)to provide facilities necessary for the enhancing ofmeditation methods to the Buddhists;\n\n(b)to collect the books and magazines of Buddhismpublished worldwide and make arrangements toaccess them easily by the Buddhists;\n\n(c)to coordinate and improve proper relation with thesocial servants, intellectuals, donators andbenevolent people and with some other similarwelfare societies and foundations in Sri Lanka bythis Corporation;\n\n(d)to print, publish and distribute the books, hand billsand magazines which may be required by theCorporation for the promotion and development ofobjects of the Corporation;\n\n(e)to cordinate with other unions, societies andorganizations having similar objects of membersof the Corporation;\n\n(f)to act in order to convince Buddhism for every oneand to take necessary actions to propagateBuddhism all over the world.\n\n4.(1) Subject to the provisions of this Act, themanagement of the affairs of the Corporation shall be carriedout by a Board of Management (hereinafter referred to as the\u201cBoard\u201d) consisting the Chairman, Vice Chairman, Secretary,the Vice Secretaries, Treasurer, Vice Treasurer and twoPatrons and other sixteen (16) members who shall beappointed in respect of the rules of the Corporation.\n\nObjects of theCorporation\n\nManagementof the affairsof theCorporation\n\n3Kelaniya Buddhist Women's Charitable Society\n\n(Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(2) Persons who were the members of executive committeeof the society at the date of coming into operation of thisAct shall consist or the first executive committee:-"
