    "chunk_text": "7.A member of the armed forces or a police officer whoknowingly, in the preparation of any document under section6 makes a statement or omits any matter which misleads inmaterial particulars in the document commits an offence.\n\nSupply ofinformation\n\nmisleadingstatementsanddocuments\n\n4 Prohibition of Anti-Personnel Mines\n\nPART II\n\nDESTRUCTION OF AN ANTI-PRESONNEL MINE\n\n9.(1) The Secretary shall make every effort to identifyor cause the identification of areas within the land owned orcontrolled by the State or government institution where anti-personnel mines are known or suspected to be emplaced.\n\n(2) Upon the identification of areas under subsection (1),the Secretary shall make best endeavours to mark theperimeter and, monitor and protect by fencing or other meansto ensure the effective exclusion of public, until all the anti-personnel mines are destroyed.\n\n10.(1) Where any person finds an anti-personnel mine,such person shall inform a member of the armed forces or apolice officer immediately.\n\n(2) The person referred to in subsection (1) shall take allreasonable steps to ensure that the anti-personnel mine willnot be exploded before a member of the armed forces orpolice officer arrives at the relevant premises.\n\n11.(1) Where a member of the armed forces or policeofficer has reasonable grounds to suspect that an anti-personnel mine is on any private premises, such officer may\u2013\n\n(a) with the consent of the person in charge of thepremises, enter and search such premises at allreasonable times;\n\n(b) make such anti-personnel mine safe from being animmediate danger;\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nObligation toprovideinformation\n\n30\n\nAnti-personnelmines ownedor possessedby theGovernment\n\nAnti-personnelmines in theState land.\n\nAnti-personnelmine inprivatepremises\n\n5 Prohibition of Anti-Personnel Mines\n\n(c) affix a warning to the anti-personnel mine or in aconspicuous position to a thing or place near suchanti-personnel mine;"
