    "chunk_text": "(Incorporation)\n\n(2) The Corporation shall have the power to do all suchother acts or things which are necessary or appropriate topromote and enhance and to the attainment of all or any ofits objects.\n\n(a)the classification of membership, fees payable bythe members of each category, admission,withdrawal, expulsion or resignation of members;\n\n(b)appointment of the officers for the executivecommittee from the Members of the Corporation;\n\n(c)functions, duties and liabilities of executivecommittee and other various officers, agents andservants; and\n\n(d)(i)the procedure to be followed at the meetingsof the Corporation and menagement of theaffairs of the Coporation.\n\n(ii)The said rules may be added to, amended orrescinded in the same manner as stated in subparagraph (01).\n\n(iii)All the members of the Corporation shall beliable to the rules of the Corporation.\n\n10.(1) The Corporation shall have its own fund.\n\n(2) All moneys received by way of gifts, donations,subscriptions, contributions or fees for and on account ofthe Corporation shall be deposited in one or more banksapproved by the Board to the credit of the Corporation.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nRules of theCorporation\n\nFund of theCorporation\n\n9Kelaniya Buddhist Women's Charitable Society\n\n(Incorporation)\n\n(3) There shall be paid out of the fund, all sums of moneyas are required to defray any expenditure incurred by theCorporation in the exercise, performance and discharge ofits powers, duties and functions under the Act.\n\n11.All debts and liabilities of the Society existing onthe day immediately preceding the date of commencementof this Act, shall be paid by the Corporation herebyconstituted and all debts due to and subscriptions andcontributions payable to the Society existing on that dayshall be paid to the Corporation for the purposes of this Act.\n\n12.The financial year of the Corporation shall be thecalendar year."
