    "chunk_text": "(3)Every regulation made by the Minister under thissection shall within three months from its publication in theGazette, be brought before Parliament for approval. Anyregulation which is not so approved shall be deemed to berescinded from the date of such disapproval but withoutprejudice to anything previously done thereunder.\n\nService ofNotices\n\nRegulations\n\n9Minimum Retirement Age of Workers\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nPART IV\n\nOFFENCES AND PENALTIES\n\n12.(1) An employer who fails to comply with a directionspecified in the notice issued by the Commissioner-Generalunder section 5, commits an offence and shall be liable onconviction after summary trial by a Magistrate to a fine notless than five thousand rupees or to an imprisonment ofeither description for a term not exceeding six months or toboth such fine and imprisonment.\n\n(2)The burden of proof that the employer has compliedwith the directions of the notice issued by the Commissioner-General under section 5 lies on such employer.\n\n(3)Upon conviction of an employer under this sectionsuch employer shall \u2013\n\n(a)pay in addition to the fine such employer is liableto pay under subsection (1), an additional fine ofone hundred rupees in respect of each day hecontinues to fail to comply with such direction afterconviction;\n\n(b)pay to the worker the wages, benefits orcompensation under paragraph (b) of subsection(3) of section 5, which would have been payable tosuch worker if such worker had been in employmentwithout being retired for the period commencingon the date specified in the notice issued undersection 5 and ending on the date of conviction ofsuch employer;\n\nPrematureretirement\n\nNon-compliancewith thedirections ofCommissioner-General\n\n30\n\n10Minimum Retirement Age of Workers\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(c)where the worker attains the minimum retirementage prior to the date of conviction of such employer,pay to the worker the wages, benefits orcompensation until the date on which he attainsthe minimum retirement age."
