    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 85]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Trade on 08th of November, 2021\n\n(Published in the Gazette on October 28, 2021)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 12.00Postage : Rs. 15. 00\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nMAHAPOLA HIGHER EDUCATION SCHOLARSHIPTRUST FUND (AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Mahapola Higher Education Scholarship Trust FundAct, No. 66 of 1981\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClauses 2 : This clause amends the long title of the Mahapola Higher Education ScholarshipTrust Fund Act, No. 66 of 1981 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d and thelegal effect of the amendment is to replace the words \u201cMAHAPOLA HIGHER EDUCATIONSCHOLARSHIP TRUST FUND ACT\u201d with the words \u201cLALITH ATHULATHMUDALIMAHAPOLA HIGHER EDUCATION SCHOLARSHIP TRUST FUND ACT\u201d.\n\nClauses 3 : This clause amends principal enactment and other written laws and the legaleffect of the amendment is to replace the words \u2013\n\n(a)\u201cMahapola Higher Education Scholarship Trust Fund Act\u201d with the words \u201cLalithAthulathmudali Mahapola Higher Education Scholarship Trust Fund Act\u201d;\n\n(b)\u201cMahapola Higher Education Scholarship Trust Fund\u201d with the words \u201cLalithAthulathmudali Mahapola Higher Education Scholarship Trust Fund\u201d.\n\nClause 4 : This clause amends section 3 of the principal enactment and the legal effect ofthe section as amended is to change the composition of the Board of Trustees of the Fund andmake provision to appoint a retired judge of the Supreme Court as the Chairman of theBoard.\n\nClause 5 : This clause amends section 15 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof the section as amended is to extend the application of that section to the Trustees of theFund."
