    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPart II of December 24, 2021\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 27.12.2021)\n\nPENAL CODE (AMENDMENT)\n\nBILL\n\nto amend the Penal Code (Chapter 19)\n\nOrdered to be published by the Minister of Justice\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 6.00Postage : Rs. 15.00\n\n2-2d\n\nThis Gazette Supplement can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nA\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2 : This clause repeals sections 285, 286 and 286A of the Penal Code(Chapter 19) and it is consequential to the introduction of the Prohibition of ObscenePublications Bill.\n\nPenal Code (Amendment)1\n\n5\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 25/2016\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE PENAL CODE ( CHAPTER 19 )\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:-\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Penal Code(Amendment) Act, No. of 2021.\n\n2.Sections 285, 286 and 286A of the Penal Code(Chapter 19) are hereby repealed.\n\n3.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nShort title\n\nRepeal ofSections285, 286and 286A ofChapter 19\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency\n\n2Penal Code (Amendment)\n\nDepartment of Government Printing"
