    "chunk_text": "The Council shall consist of five Honorary Office bearers(President, President Elect, Immediate Past President,\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nMembership\n\nManagementof the affairsof theCorporation\n\nInstitution of Building Services Engineering &Technology of Sri Lanka (Incorporation)6\n\nIf a vacancy is created due to the death of a member,holding office the Council shall have the right to nominate asuitable member to fill the vacancy thus created. However,in the case of the President, the President Elect shall takeover the office of President.\n\nMembers for the first Council of IBSE & TSL immediatelyafter incorporation shall be nominated by the Council of\u201cLanka Association of Building Service Engineers\u201d existingimmediately prior to incorporation.\n\n6.(1) To acquire, hold, take or give on lease, hire,mortgage, pledge, sell and exchange, or otherwise to alienate,encumber or dispose of any immovable or movable propertyfor the purpose of the Institution.\n\n(2) To enter into and perform or carry out, whether directlyor indirectly, through and official agents authorized in thatbehalf by the institution all such contracts or agreements asmay be necessary for the attainment of the objectives or theexercise of powers of the Institution.\n\n(3) To invest its funds and to maintain Fixed/TermDeposits, Current and Savings Accounts in any bank or inany recognised trust fund or funds.\n\n(4) To advance or lend and to borrow money for thepurpose of the Institution in such a manner and such securityas the Institution may think fit.\n\n(5) To levy fees, subscriptions and contributions in respectof membership, admission to membership and admission to\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nGeneralpowers of theCorporation\n\n7Institution of Building Services Engineering &Technology of Sri Lanka (Incorporation)\n\ncourses, examination, exhibitions etc. conducted by theInstitution."
