    "chunk_text": "BE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic Socialist\n\nRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Revocation ofIrrevocable Deeds of Gift on the ground of Gross Ingratitude\n\n2.Section 2 of the Revocation of Irrevocable Deeds of\n\nGift on the ground of Gross Ingratitude Act, No. 5 of 2017(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is hereby\n\nrepealed and the following section substituted therefor:\u2013\n\n2. The revocation of an irrevocable deed\n\nof gift on the ground of gross ingratitude shall\n\nonly be made on an order made by a competentcourt, in an action filed by the donor of such\n\ndeed against the donee to have the said deed\n\nrevoked.\u201d.\n\n3.Section 3 of the principal enactment is hereby\n\nrepealed and the following section substituted therefor:\u2013\n\n3. Court shall not entertain an action\n\nreferred to in section 2, unless it is filed within\n\nthree years from the date on which cause of\n\naction arose.\u201d.\n\nReplacementof section 2of Act, No. 5of 2017\n\n\u201cRevocationofirrevocabledeed of gift\n\nReplacementof section 3of theprincipalenactment\u201cTime periodwithin whichaction shallbe filed\n\n2 Revocation of Irrevocable Deeds of Gifton the ground of Gross Ingratitude (Amendment)\n\n\u201cProcrdure tobe followedin theregistration oflis pendens5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nReplacementof section 4of theprincipalenactment\n\n4.Section 4 of the principal enactment is herebyrepealed and the following section substituted therefor:\u2013\n\n4. (1) The plaintiff, in an action institutedunder the provisions of this Act shall file orcause to be filed in the District Court with theplaint, an application for registration oflis pendens \u2013\n\n(a) addressed to the Registrar of Landsor the Registrar of Title as the casemay be, in the relevant LandRegistry or in the relevant TitleRegistry as the case may be in whichthe irrevocable deed of gift soughtto be revoked was registered; and\n\n(b) shall contain the correct priorregistration number where theirrevocable deed of gift sought to berevoked has been previouslyregistered."
